    "name": "Gym Challenge (Japan)"
  },
  "description": {
    "text": "In 2008 Japan's Official Pokémon Card Gyms began holding a Gym Challenge to launch each new expansion. From 15 March to 20 April the tournaments for Cry from the Mysterious, Temple of Anger and the Heatran vs Regigigas battle starter pack gave first place Infernape LV.X 071/DP-P, the participation card of the Winter Challenge. From 10 July those for Intense Fight in the Destroyed Sky (Stormfront in English) gave every player a Magnemite and the top players a cosmos holo Luxury Ball, and from 12 July to 31 August everyone who visited a shop holding Gym Challenge events got Buizel, one of the 13 cards of that summer's Collection Challenge.\n\nFor Galactic's Conquest, released on 10 October, every player got Bronzong G, the top three or four, depending on the age group, Cyrus's Conspiracy, and each winner the 2007 gold Victory Medal. For Bonds to the End of Time, on sale from 26 December, every player got Alakazam E4 and Team Galactic's Invention G-109 SP Radar and the top finishers Luxray GL, all three with the Gym Challenge logo in the text box.",
